# # User / Account Requirements

#

# - A user can create an account.

# - A user can log into an existing account.

# - A user can log out.

# - A user account has a unique username.

# - A user account stores an email address.

# - Passwords must be securely stored rather than saved as plain text.

# - The system prevents duplicate usernames.

# - The system prevents duplicate email accounts.

# - A user can view their profile.

# - A user's profile shows the reviews they have submitted.

# - A user can edit basic profile information.

# - A user can delete their account.

#

# # Restaurant Requirements

#

# - The system displays a list of restaurants.

# - Each restaurant has a name.

# - Each restaurant has an address or location.

# - Each restaurant has a dedicated restaurant page.

# - A restaurant page displays its average fry rating.

# - A restaurant page displays all reviews for that restaurant's fries.

# - A restaurant can have a description.

# - A restaurant can display a picture or logo.

# - Users can search for restaurants by name.

# - Users can browse all restaurants.

# - Users can add a restaurant that does not currently exist.

# - The system prevents obvious duplicate restaurant entries.

# - Restaurants can be sorted alphabetically.

#

# # Fry Information Requirements

#

# - Each restaurant can have at least one type of fries listed.

# - A fry listing contains the name or type of fries.

# - A fry listing can contain a description.

# - A fry listing can display an image.

# - Each fry listing displays its average rating.

# - The application displays the number of ratings submitted for a fry.

# - Users can view all reviews associated with a specific fry.

# - Fries can be identified by style, such as shoestring, steak, waffle, curly, or crinkle-cut.

# - Fries can be marked as seasoned or unseasoned.

# - Fries can have an optional price listed.

#

# # Rating Requirements

#

# - A logged-in user can rate fries.

# - Ratings use a 1–5 star scale.

# - A user cannot submit a rating below 1 star.

# - A user cannot submit a rating above 5 stars.

# - The system calculates the average rating for fries.

# - The average rating automatically updates after a new rating is submitted.

# - Ratings display to one decimal place.

# - A user can change their rating.

# - A user can remove their rating.

# - A user can only submit one rating per fry item, though they may edit it later.

#

# # Review Requirements

#

# - A logged-in user can write a review.

# - A review contains a star rating.

# - A review contains written text.

# - A review displays the reviewer's username.

# - A review displays the date it was submitted.

# - Reviews are displayed on the restaurant page.

# - Reviews are displayed newest-first by default.

# - A user can edit their own review.

# - A user can delete their own review.

# - Users cannot edit another user's review.

# - Users cannot delete another user's review.

# - Reviews have a maximum character limit.

# - Empty reviews cannot be submitted if written comments are required.

# - The system asks the user for confirmation before deleting a review.

#

# # Fry-Specific Rating Requirements

#

# - A reviewer can rate fry crispiness.

# - A reviewer can rate fry seasoning.

# - A reviewer can rate fry texture.

# - A reviewer can rate fry freshness.

# - A reviewer can rate portion size.

# - A reviewer can rate value for the price.

# - A reviewer can rate dipping-sauce selection.

# - The system displays an average crispiness score.

# - The system displays an average seasoning score.

# - The system displays an overall fry score.

# - A review can indicate whether the fries were eaten dine-in, takeout, or delivery.

#

# # Search and Filtering Requirements

#

# - Users can search for a restaurant by name.

# - Search results update based on the user's search query.

# - Users can filter restaurants by minimum fry rating.

# - Users can sort restaurants by highest fry rating.

# - Users can sort restaurants by lowest fry rating.

# - Users can sort restaurants alphabetically.

# - Users can filter fries by fry style.

# - Users can search for a specific type of fry.

# - The system displays a message when no search results are found.

# - Users can clear filters and return to the full restaurant list.

# - Users can search for restaraunts within a certain radius of their location

# - Users can search for fries within a price range

# # Homepage Requirements

#

# - The application has a homepage.

# - The homepage displays the application's name and branding.

# - The homepage contains a restaurant search bar.

# - The homepage displays several recently reviewed restaurants.

# - The homepage displays highly rated fries.

# - The homepage provides navigation to the restaurant list.

# - The homepage provides login and registration options for logged-out users.

# - The homepage provides account and profile options for logged-in users.

#

# # Navigation and User Interface Requirements

#

# - Every page contains consistent navigation.

# - Users can return to the homepage from the navigation bar.

# - Users can access restaurant search from the navigation bar.

# - Users can access their profile from the navigation bar.

# - Buttons clearly indicate their intended action.

# - Forms identify required fields.

# - The application provides confirmation after successfully submitting a review.

# - The application provides an error message when a form cannot be submitted.

# - The application has a consistent visual design.

# - Restaurant ratings are visually represented with stars.

# - Pages remain readable on both desktop and mobile screens.

# - Users can navigate the major features without using the browser back button.

#

# # Data and Database Requirements

#

# - User information is stored in a database.

# - Restaurant information is stored in a database.

# - Fry information is stored in a database.

# - Review information is stored in a database.

# - Ratings are associated with the user who submitted them.

# - Ratings are associated with the correct restaurant or fry item.

# - Reviews remain available after restarting the application.

# - Deleting a review removes it from the database.

# - Updating a review updates the existing database entry rather than creating a duplicate.

# - Restaurant average ratings are calculated using stored review data.

#

# # Validation and Error Handling Requirements

#

# - Required fields cannot be submitted empty.

# - Invalid login credentials produce an appropriate error message.

# - Invalid email formats are rejected during registration.

# - Ratings outside the allowed range are rejected.

# - The application handles nonexistent restaurant URLs gracefully.

# - The application displays a 404 or error page for invalid pages.

# - Users must be logged in before submitting reviews.

# - Users must be logged in before editing reviews.

# - Users can only modify content they created.

# - Database errors do not expose sensitive technical information to users.

#

# # Nonfunctional Requirements

#

# - Normal pages should load within a reasonable amount of time.

# - User passwords must not be stored as plain text.

# - The application should support modern desktop web browsers.

# - The user interface should be understandable without special training.

# - Text should have sufficient contrast against its background.

# - Forms should clearly communicate errors to users.

# - The application should maintain consistent formatting across pages.

# - The database should maintain relationships between users, restaurants, fries, and reviews.

# - The application should prevent unauthorized users from accessing protected operations.

# - The application should continue functioning correctly when multiple reviews exist for the same restaurant.
